(:room
 :id "tea-table"
 :title "Lawn and Tea Table"
 :body
 ((:p "The motor turns in at the lodge gates and the old house comes into view. Before tea, John introduces you to Evelyn Howard in the garden: blunt, sunburnt, vigorous, and already warning you that usefulness at Styles comes with thorns.")
  (:p "She leads you round the house to the lawn, where tea is laid under a wide tree. Mary Cavendish rises from a basket chair with a stillness that catches you off guard; Emily Inglethorp presides kindly but completely; Alfred hovers near her; Cynthia comes bright from hospital work; Evelyn watches Alfred with open contempt.")
  (:p "You are still only a guest, but the household has begun arranging itself before you like evidence: old affection, new marriage, money, dependence, charm, resentment, and a politeness too thin to hide the cracks.")
  (:when (:marked? :clue-evie-warning)
   (:p "Evelyn's warning about Alfred hangs in the air, blunt enough to seem honest."))
  (:when (:marked? :clue-cynthia-dispensary)
   (:p "Cynthia's dispensary work gives her brightness a sharper edge: she handles medicines every day."))
  (:choice
   :options
   ((:once
     :id :styles-ask-evelyn
     (:option
      :label "Ask Evelyn why she distrusts Alfred"
      :do ((:mark :clue-evie-warning)
           (:say "Evelyn says Alfred is a dangerous man, and says it as if contradiction would be indecent."))))
    (:once
     :id :styles-ask-cynthia-tea
     (:option
      :label "Ask Cynthia about the dispensary"
      :do ((:mark :clue-cynthia-dispensary)
           (:say "Cynthia laughs about her work, but the names of drugs and poisons come easily to her."))))
    (:once
     :id :styles-ask-mary-poisons
     (:option
      :label "Ask Mary about poisons"
      :do ((:mark :clue-mary-poison-talk)
           (:say "Mary speaks lightly of poisons, then notices Hastings noticing."))))
    (:option
     :label "Retire for the night"
     :do (:go "night-crisis"))))))
